DevOps Interview Preparation Docker
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 6 

Production-Level Containerization

For 2–4 years experience, interviewers expect you to optimize images, secure containers, and troubleshoot production issues, not just run containers.

🔹 Docker Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• What is Docker and why is it used in production?
• Docker architecture (Client, Daemon, Registry)
• Image vs container — real-world difference
• What happens when you run docker run?
• CMD vs ENTRYPOINT
• COPY vs ADD
• What are Docker layers and why do they matter?
• How do you reduce Docker image size?
• What is a multi-stage Docker build?
• Dockerfile best practices
• How do you handle environment variables in Docker?
• How do you manage secrets in Docker?
• Docker networking types
• Docker volumes vs bind mounts
• How do you persist data in containers?
• Docker logging drivers
• How do you monitor Docker containers?
• Docker security best practices
• Docker vs Podman
🔹 Real-World Docker Scenarios

• Docker image size is very large — how will you optimize it?
• Container keeps restarting — how will you debug?
• Application works locally but fails in container — why?
• How do you scan Docker images for vulnerabilities?
• Secrets accidentally baked into image — what will you do?
• Docker container consuming high memory — how to fix?
• How do you implement rollback with Docker images?

🔹 Best Practices (2–4 yrs Level)

• Use multi-stage builds
• Use minimal base images (alpine, distroless)
• Never run containers as root
• Use .dockerignore
• Tag images properly
• Scan images before pushing
• Push images to private registry

Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “We use multi-stage builds, minimal base images, and image scanning in our pipelines”
you already sound like a strong 2–4 years DevOps engineer.
